# Byte-exact reference data. These are inputs to tests that compare hashes, base64
# SPKIs and certificate chains; a line-ending rewrite on checkout would change the
# bytes without changing anything a human would notice.
#
# Encountered for real on 2026-10-07: git warned "LF will be replaced by CRLF" when
# the Redmi attestation fixtures were first committed.

supabase/functions/oracle/fixtures/** -text
supabase/functions/oracle/fixtures/**/*.der binary
supabase/functions/oracle/fixtures/**/*.pem -text

# Deliberately narrow. This machine has core.autocrlf=true; adding `* text eol=lf`
# rules for source files would rewrite the working copy of every .kt/.ts in the repo
# mid-plan to solve a problem nobody reported. Revisit only if the repo goes
# multi-OS (plan Task 19 makes it public).

# Never let a build artifact or keystore material sneak in.
*.keystore binary
*.jks binary
*.apk binary
